      "section_title": "LunchBox: A powerful Plugin to generate panels and other functions.",
      "section_number": 1,
      "teaching_text": "1- LunchBox: A powerful Plugin to generate panels and other functions.\r\n\r\n- \"Isotrim\" and \"Divide Surface\" components are useful tools in Grasshopper. However when the design intention becomes more complex, involving diamond or hexagonal divisions, building a definition manually in Grasshopper may become time consuming.\r\n\r\nLunchBox is a very useful plugin that provides ready made components for multi-purpose surface division. It also provides other functions such as Surface Flatness test and more.\r\n\r\nUsing LunchBox:\r\n\r\n- Build a Surface in Rhino with 4 corners, using the \"SrfPt\".\r\n- Turn on the Control Points and make the surface unplanar.\r\n- Reference the Surface in Grasshopper.\r\n\r\n- Use the following LunchBox compnents from the Panels Tab:\r\n1- Quad Panels\r\n2- Random Quad Panels\r\n3- Skewed Quads\r\n4- Hexagon Cells\r\n5- Diamond Panels\r\n6- Triangular Panels A\r\n7- Triangular Panels B\r\n8- Triangular Panels C\r\n\r\n- Use the following LunchBox compnents from the Structure Tab:\r\n1- Grid Structure\r\n2- Hexagonal Structure\r\n3- Diagrid Structure\r\n4- Braced Grid 1-D Structure\r\n5- Braced Grid 2-D Structure",
      "teaching_panel_id": "C12",
      "additional_teaching_panels": [],
      "sub_annotations": [],
      "concepts_taught": [
        "Isotrim",
        "Divide Surface",
        "SrfPt",
        "Reference the Surface in Grasshopper."
